# fisher-5sg.5, 2026-11-25. See README.md for derivation.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# fisher-8ie, fisher-r6y D20, D24, D28 and D41, fisher-5sg decisions 2–6 and 10.
# Perft: expectations/perft.epd. Independent minimax: python-chess 1.11.2.
# Full info spelling: Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), as cited in expectations/README.md.
# fisher-4yn.1, 2026-11-25: every node total at depth 2 or more reads
# {nodes}. Once the search makes cutoffs, such a total depends on the order
# Position::legal_moves returns moves in, which nobody chose (fisher-4yn,
# D36 and D38). Scores, depths, principal variations, bestmove and the
# depth-1 totals (the number of legal moves at the root) stay exact. A node
# count in these comments describes the search without cutoffs before it.
> position startpos
> go nodes 0
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 19
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 20
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 21
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 439
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> go nodes 440
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The only legal move pins the zero-limit answer (D20).
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8g8

# One node short of depth 5, then the exact cumulative limit.
> go nodes 3137
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< bestmove h8g8

> go nodes 3138
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< info depth 5 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv h8g8 h6g7
< bestmove h8g8

# The sole node of depth 1 uses the entire limit. Hold the move (decision 5).
> go infinite nodes 1
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
< readyok
# Rule 8. Reject both commands and keep the original position.
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
< info string {message:position rejected: waiting for stop}
> go nodes 1
< info string {message:go rejected: waiting for stop}
> stop
# D24. The following go uses the retained position.
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8g8
< bestmove h8g8
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go nodes 0
< bestmove h8h7

# The terminal response precedes the zero limit.
> position fen 7k/6Q1/5K2/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go nodes 0
< info depth 0 score mate 0
< bestmove 0000

> quit
! exit
